Observable, testable outcomes, one unchecked checklist item each. Each becomes
a test, and the reviewer reports each one as met or not met. For example:
{{ if eq .Framework "aws-queue-ts" -}}
a message `{"id": "lamp-1", "delete": true}` deletes the item, a later message
for `lamp-1` stores it again, and the function's role may delete items but
still not scan the table.
{{- else if eq .Framework "aws-schedule-ts" -}}
a run at 03:00 UTC records its scheduled time and when it finished, a
run delivered twice for the same scheduled time is recorded once, and the
function's role may put runs but still not delete them.
{{- else if eq .Framework "aws-static-site-ts" -}}
a name of only spaces gets the plain greeting, and the page says so in its
`aria-live` paragraph.
{{- else -}}
`DELETE /items/{id}` answers 204 and a later `GET` answers 404, and the
{{ if eq .Framework "aws-ec2-ts" }}instances'{{ else if eq .Framework "aws-fargate-ts" }}task's{{ else }}function's{{ end }} role may delete items but still not scan the table.
{{- end }}
